# Copy to .env (gitignored) and adjust as needed — you usually need NOTHING here.
#
# By default `make up` joins the shared Traefik proxy and the demo is reachable
# at a stable URL: http://accrue.localhost/admin. No port-picking, no collisions
# with your other lib demos. Run `make proxy` once to start the shared proxy.
#
# If the proxy isn't running, `make up` still works: Docker auto-picks a free
# ephemeral host port and the banner prints the fallback URL.

# Stable hostname the proxy routes to. Default accrue.localhost. Override to run
# a second checkout side by side (or set it via `make up INSTANCE=accrue-foo`,
# which derives ACCRUE_HOST=accrue-foo.localhost for you).
# ACCRUE_HOST=accrue.localhost

# Compose project name = instance identity (isolates networks, volumes,
# containers, and the Traefik route). The Makefile sets this from INSTANCE.
# COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=accrue-host

# Pin a FIXED fallback host port instead of ephemeral — only needed if you skip
# the proxy AND require a stable port (e.g. an OAuth redirect URI).
# ACCRUE_HOST_DOCKER_PORT=4010

# ACCRUE_HOST_DOCKER_BIND=127.0.0.1   # set 0.0.0.0 to reach the fallback from other devices
# PGPORT=5432                          # only used by docker-compose.override.yml (DB GUI)
